00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:10.840
Of course we're not giving the thumbs up to murder,

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:17.040
but Black's point is that when performed with the right craft, style, and force violence can have an almost

00:05:17.140 --> 00:05:22.600
transcendent effect on its viewers. This idea that something can leave us in awe and

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:28.940
transcend understanding is what philosopher Immanuel Kant referred to as the sublime or the State of Mind

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:36.180
created when a certain experience stops being an object of our judgment and starts controlling it. Starting to sound familiar?

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:42.040
Like monster horror, the sublime has the power to violate the purpose in respect of the judgment and to do

00:05:42.140 --> 00:05:47.840
violence to the imagination. It works through a process of categorical violation; breaking down the

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:50.060
divisions between our commonly held beliefs.

00:05:50.069 --> 00:05:56.509
So how does the sublime in berserk transform us? By forcing us to reconsider our traditionally held ideas.

